    "stride_ceiling": "gapless tiling needs +/-C mod stride = Z_stride, hence stride <= 2*rows-1; C=[R,2R-1] with stride 2R-1 reaches the ceiling (0 holes in enumeration, exhaustive for R<=6)",
    "current_layout_slack": "default layout (C=[1,R], stride R) covers every offset exactly twice - the mirror redundancy is monetized by --giant-stride 2R-1 on heads [R,2R-1]: half the giants",
    "lambda_tiling": "orbit multipliers do NOT extend gapless tiling: measured residue densities < 1 at stride 3R-1 and 6R-1 (holes guaranteed)",
    "partner_scatter": "orbit partners of heads [1,H] never land in the swept window (0 in all measured H), partner coverage is worthless for contiguous sweeps",
    "row_payload": "scalar column is implied for consecutive heads (65->33 B); truncated key b=64 adds 8.4e-11 relative work at H=4M full window (65->8 B); combined with mirror stride ~16x bytes*giants",
